<title>USA: Odyssey Partners to sell unit for $675 mln - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Odyssey Partners to sell unit for $675 mln - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Odyssey Partners has agreed to sell its Williams Scotsman unit to two financial firms for $675 million in cash and assumed debt, the Wall Street Journal said in Monday's electronic edition.</p>
<p>The two firms jointly acquiring the unit were the Cypress Group and Robert Bass's Keystone Inc, the newspaper said, citing people familiar with the situation.</p>
<p>Odyssey is a closely-held investment firm based in New York and Scotsman leases mobile-office units, the paper said.</p>
<p>Odyssey was not immediately available to comment.</p>
</text>
